# Security Rules

## Authentication and Authorization

- Check session on EVERY request to protected resources
- Use proxy (src/proxy.ts) for route protection

## Data Validation

- ALL input data validated through Zod 4.0
- Never trust client data
- Validate on server even if client validation exists
- Use schema for query params, body, params

## SQL Injection Protection

- NEVER use raw SQL queries without necessity
- When using raw SQL (Kysely.sql) - always use parameterized queries
- Escape all user data

## XSS Protection

- NEVER use dangerouslySetInnerHTML without sanitization
- Use DOMPurify for HTML sanitization
- Content Security Policy (CSP) headers REQUIRED
- Use nonce for inline scripts

## CSRF Protection

- Next.js built-in CSRF protection for Server Actions
- For API routes use CSRF tokens
- Check Origin header for state-changing operations

## Secrets and Keys

- NEVER commit secrets to repository
- Use .env.local for local secrets
- All secrets through process.env
- In production use secret vaults (Vault, AWS Secrets)

## Logging

- DO NOT log sensitive data (passwords, tokens, PII)
- Log all authentication attempts
- Log all security errors
- Use structured logging

## Rate Limiting

- Apply rate limiting to all public APIs
- Limit login attempts (5 attempts / 15 minutes)
- Limit API requests (100 requests / minute)

## File Uploads

- Limit file sizes (max 10MB)
- Check MIME types
- Use virus scanning for user uploads
- Don't save files with executable extensions
